3.text:
With the origin included put $S_{n}=\{0,X_{1},\dots ,X_{n}\}$,
$X_{i}=T_{i}e_{J_{i}}$, $T_{i}\sim U[-1,1]$ i.i.d., 
${\mathbb P}\{J_{i}=k\}=n^{-1}$ i.i.d.  On $\{J_{1},\dots ,J_{n}{\rm
distinct}\}$

$|\det[X_{1}\dots X_{n}]|=\prod_{i}|T_{i}|$, 
${\mathbb P}\{J_{1},\dots ,J_{n}{\rm distinct}\}=n!/n^{n}$ and with
$E|T|=1/2$

\begin{equation*}
E{\rm Vol}_{n}
   =\frac1{n!}(E|T|)^{n}\frac{n!}{n^{n}}
   =2^{-n}n^{-n},\qquad E{\rm Vol}_{1}=1/2 ,
\end{equation*}
the unconditional volume on the cross
$\displaystyle \bigcup_{k=1}^{n}e_{k}[-1,1]$.  Put
$U_{i}=|T_{i}|\sim U[0,1]$ and

\begin{equation*}
s=E\sqrt{U_{1}^{2}+U_{2}^{2}}
   =\int_{0}^{1}\!\!\int_{0}^{1}\!\sqrt{u^{2}+v^{2}}\,du\,dv
   =\frac{\sqrt2+{\rm arsinh}1}{3}
   =\frac{\sqrt2+\log\!\left(1+\sqrt2\right)}{3}=0.765195716\ldots ,
\end{equation*}
$L:=3s=\sqrt2+\log\!\left(1+\sqrt2\right)=2.295587149\ldots$,
$E|T_{1}-T_{2}|=2/3$, $E\|X\|=1/2$.  For two independent cross points

\begin{equation*}
E_{p}(n)=E\|X_{1}-X_{2}\|
       =\frac1n\frac23+\Bigl(1-\frac1n\Bigr)s
       =\frac{2+(n-1)L}{3n},
\end{equation*}
and for the $n+1$ points of $S_{n}$

\begin{equation*}
\bar D_{n}
 =\frac{nE\|X\|+\binom n2E_{p}(n)}{\binom{n+1}{2}}
 =\frac{1+(n-1)E_{p}(n)}{n+1}
 =\frac{5n-2+L(n-1)^{2}}{3n(n+1)},\qquad \bar D_{1}=1/2,
\end{equation*}
$\bar D_{n}\to s$.  Hence with $R_{n}=E{\rm Vol}_{n}/\bar D_{n}$

\begin{equation*}
R_{n}
   =\frac{2^{-n}n^{-n}}{\bar D_{n}}
   =\frac{3(n+1)2^{-n}n^{\,1-n}}{5n-2+L(n-1)^{2}},\qquad R_{1}=1,
\end{equation*}
i.e. $R_{n}=3n(n+1)(2n)^{-n}\!\left[L(n-1)^{2}+5n-2\right]^{-1}$,
$R_{n}=O[(2n)^{-n}]$.

In particular

* $R_{1}=1.000000$,
* $R_{2}=1.125/(8+L)=0.109270\ldots$,
* $R_{3}=0.166666\ldots/(13+4L)=0.007513\ldots$,
* $R_{4}=0.0146484375/(18+9L)=3.79\times10^{-4}$,
* $R_{5}=1.5\times10^{-5}$,

and $R_{n}<10^{-6}$ for $n\ge 6$.  The tail is therefore negligible
and

\begin{equation*}
S_{N}=\sum_{n=1}^{N}R_{n}
     =1+0.109270+0.007513+0.000379+0.000015+\cdots .
\end{equation*}

With the exact $s$,

\begin{equation*}
S_{\infty}
 =\sum_{n\ge1}\frac{3(n+1)2^{-n}n^{\,1-n}}
        {5n-2+\bigl[\sqrt2+\log(1+\sqrt2)\bigr](n-1)^{2}}
 =1.11718\ldots,
\end{equation*}
so that $R_{1}+R_{2}+R_{3}=1.1168$ already gives the three-decimal
value.  To three decimals

$S_{\infty}\approx1.117$, $S_{\infty}\approx1.12$ in round reporting,
the $n=1$ term being $1$ and $R_{2}+R_{3}+\cdots\approx0.117$ the whole
with-replacement remainder.  This is the i.i.d. uniform-on-the-union
$\bigcup_{k}e_{k}(-1,1)$ origin-included normalisation.  The $P=1$
fixed-axis bijection $E{\rm Vol}_{n}=2^{-n}/n!$ gives the familiar
$R_{n}^{0}=(n+1)2^{-n}/[n!\,(1+(n-1)s)]$ and $\sum_{n}R_{n}^{0}\approx
1.2497\approx1.25$, the $n!/n^{n}$ collision factor being the only
difference between the two readings. ∎

